course: dictionary
lesson: 11781
title: Beeswax: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Beeswax» is made of two words, bee and wax, and it has a few meanings. You can work out which one you need from the sentence around it.
explain: «The honeycomb was built from beeswax by the busy bees.» Here beeswax is the yellow wax that bees make. «Mum rubbed beeswax polish into the old table.» Now beeswax means the wax used to make polish. The words around it show you the right meaning.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does it make sense? Some words also have a playful meaning. «"What did you buy me?" "None of your beeswax!" laughed Sam.» Here it means none of your business, so Sam is joking and will not tell.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Beeswax» is the yellow wax that honeybees make to build their honeycomb.
fact: People use beeswax to make candles, polish, crayons and lip balm.
fact: In informal US speech, «none of your beeswax» means «none of your business».
fact: In science lessons, honeybee workers make wax from glands on their bodies and build hexagon-shaped cells.
exercise: «The bees made golden beeswax to build their honeycomb.» What is beeswax in this sentence? | *The yellow wax bees make | A type of flower | The lid on a jam pot | A kind of honey sold in jars
exercise: «Grandma lit a beeswax candle for the dinner table.» What is beeswax used for here? | To paint a fence | To feed the bees | To cook pasta | *To make a candle
exercise: «"What did you buy me?" "None of your beeswax!" laughed Sam.» What does beeswax mean in this phrase? | *Business, so Sam will not tell | A yellow wax for building honeycomb | A sweet treat from the shop | A bright red crayon
test: «Lena rubbed beeswax into the wooden chair until it shone.» What is the beeswax used for in this sentence? | *Polish | Sticking paper together | Building a hive | Making honey
test: «Ben's lip balm smelled of honey because it was made with beeswax.» What is beeswax in this sentence? | A jar of honey | Wax used to build a hive | *A wax used in lip balm | A type of bee
exam: «Mia polished her bike with beeswax, and it gleamed.» Which meaning fits best? | *The wax used as a polish | A playful way to say none of your business | A type of bee that makes honey | The cells inside a honeycomb
